    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e6b5dbc9_01c5aafc",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/imsphone/ImsPhone.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1528,
      "author": {
        "id": 1660874
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-17T06:07:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think current initiateSilentRedial is enough to support both cases.\nTo use initiateSilentRedialForEmergency, emergency redial should be checked before calling it.\nAnd even keep initiateSilentRedial for normal call, it should be modified to deliver SilentRedialParam.\nCould you confirm it again?",
      "parentUuid": "8244905c_ebd5fd34",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1528,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 1528,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "86cf4d212afdf0be9c33143b4fe42225155729ad",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "53a79866_7cf7c036",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/imsphone/ImsPhone.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1528,
      "author": {
        "id": 1098053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-18T17:39:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It removes the need for passing in isEmergency into initateSilentRedial, since it will always be false in the case that initiateSilentRedial() is called. By splitting it into two methods initiateSilentRedial and initiateSilentRedialForEmergency, you do not need to track the isEmergency boolean and pass in a unspecified service category.\n\nSplitting into two increases readability, but I am fine with the current structure.",
      "parentUuid": "e6b5dbc9_01c5aafc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1528,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 1528,
        "endChar": 24
      },
